 # Combo variant of b9e38dc0 (index 21)
 # combo_spec: D11/0+D19/2
 # Name: 孤立像素异色+颜色匹配关联
-#
-# Design analysis for the fused variant
-# -------------------------------------
-# a) Concrete behavior:
-#    Each puzzle contains two wall sprites.  Every sprite keeps the original
-#    funnel behavior: a small interior source blob flood-fills the enclosed
-#    pocket and then radiates outward through the opening.  In addition, each
-#    wall color appears once more as a detached singleton placed near the other
-#    sprite's radiate zone.  Example: a blue wall with a red source may coexist
-#    with a yellow wall with a green source; the detached blue pixel is placed
-#    near the yellow funnel, but in the output it still moves in the blue
-#    wall's outward direction and paints a blue trail to the edge.
-# b) Complexity calibration:
-#    Two sprites are enough to make the color association visible without
-#    overloading the grid.  The detached pixels are cross-placed so proximity
-#    suggests the wrong sprite, while color repetition with the wall suggests
-#    the correct one.  Using exactly one detached pixel per wall color keeps
-#    the rule repeated and legible.
-# c) Broken original assumptions:
-#    The original solver assumed one dominant wall color and one closest fill
-#    color.  That fails here because wall colors are split across two sprites
-#    and each wall color also appears as a detached singleton.  The new solver
-#    therefore identifies large monochrome wall components by connectivity,
-#    assigns one source color to each wall independently, and treats tiny extra
-#    components of a wall color as movable isolated pixels rather than as wall.
-# d) Placement legality:
-#    The generator places one vertical-radiating and one horizontal-radiating
-#    wall in opposite corners, grows a seed blob strictly inside each enclosure,
-#    computes the nominal radiate zones, and only then inserts the detached
-#    pixels on background cells with a clear straight ray to the edge.
-# e) Visual observability:
-#    The detached pixels always share color with a wall but not with the wall's
-#    source blob.  Because they are intentionally closer to the other sprite,
